# Data conversion between kibibyte and megabyte

Verifies direct data conversion between kibibyte and megabyte in both directions. Forward, converting 1KiB to 0.0010MB with a fractional finer-to-coarser scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5KiB yields 0.0015MB; backward, converting 1MB to 976.5625KiB with a fractional coarser-to-finer scale promotes the integer result to decimal, while 1.5MB yields 1464.8437KiB.

>>> source
forward_whole: int = 1KiB
print(forward_whole->to(MB))
forward_fractional: decimal = 1.5KiB
print(forward_fractional->to(MB))
backward_whole: int = 1MB
print(backward_whole->to(KiB))
backward_fractional: decimal = 1.5MB
print(backward_fractional->to(KiB))

<<< stdout
0.0010MB
0.0015MB
976.5625KiB
1464.8437KiB

<<< stderr
